Subject: [PATCH 032/154] feat: stand up the Rust core behind a C ABI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The model is moving to Rust (decision-3). This is the scaffolding: a crate
that builds under GN, a hand-written C header, and nothing behind it yet.

The crate has two copies. rust/atrium-core in the Atrium repo is the one you
edit; this one is a copy, because GN cannot build anything outside its own
checkout and the sync server has no Atrium repo at all. `make rust-verify`
fails when they drift.

cbindgen is not vendored, so include/atrium_core.h is written by hand and
nothing generates it. Two tests hold the header and the crate together:
atrium_core_abi_unittest.cc compares the header's ATRIUM_CORE_ABI_VERSION
against what the linked library reports, and a cargo test reads the header
directly so the same check runs without a Chromium checkout.

The header's define is unsigned. A bare 1 is an int, and comparing it to the
uint32_t the function returns is a -Wsign-compare error under -Werror.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/DEPS | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/DEPS b/chrome/browser/DEPS
index 60010fad1fd64..579824478d9f0 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/DEPS
+++ b/chrome/browser/DEPS
@@ -491,6 +491,9 @@ include_rules = [
   "+services/viz/public",
   "+services/viz/privileged",
   "+skia/ext",
+  # First-party Atrium code. It sits under third_party only because GN cannot
+  # build a crate that lives outside the checkout.
+  "+third_party/atrium",
   "+third_party/boringssl/src/include",
   "+third_party/content_analysis_sdk",
   "+third_party/crashpad",
